IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-seat`

-- Worked cases for er5-seat (the claimant's seat, Employment Insurance Regulations Parts IV and V): at least one case for every question, written in the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Every argument list and every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Regulations (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1394-1708), beside the assertion, before the run.
-- Figures the text does not give (a table of Schedule II.x, the days a section came into force, the rates and hours) are invented for the case and said so in its comment.
-- A case marked 'not covered' asserts NOTHING: the text does not answer.

§ `Reg 77 -- Pilot Project No. 1, periodic claims (ended in 1999)`

-- Q1. Pregnancy benefits only: the waiting period (March 2 to 15, 1997) lies inside the s 22(2) period (February 2 to August 2, 1997), which is therefore the period of eligibility.
#ASSERT `What is my period of eligibility for Pilot Project No. 1 if I claim for pregnancy or for a child` (YearMonthDay 1997 3 2) (YearMonthDay 1997 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 1997 2 2) (YearMonthDay 1997 8 2) FALSE (YearMonthDay 1997 8 3) (YearMonthDay 1998 8 1) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 1997 2 2), (YearMonthDay 1997 8 2))

-- Q1. Neither pregnancy nor child benefits are claimed: no aggregate.
#ASSERT `What is my period of eligibility for Pilot Project No. 1 if I claim for pregnancy or for a child` (YearMonthDay 1997 3 2) (YearMonthDay 1997 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 1997 2 2) (YearMonthDay 1997 8 2) FALSE (YearMonthDay 1997 8 3) (YearMonthDay 1998 8 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q2. An apprenticeship course from September 1 to October 24, 1997: the period of attendance is the period of eligibility.
#ASSERT `What is my period of eligibility for Pilot Project No. 1 if I attend an apprenticeship course` (YearMonthDay 1997 9 1) (YearMonthDay 1997 10 24) TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 1997 9 1), (YearMonthDay 1997 10 24))

-- Q3. Lives in Canada, asking in December 1996, made an initial claim, period of eligibility June 30, 1996 to January 10, 1997, claims every week.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to take part in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1996 12 1) TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30) (YearMonthDay 1997 1 10) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q3. The period of eligibility ends June 27, 1999, a day after the last day allowed (June 26, 1999).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to take part in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1998 12 1) TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1998 6 30) (YearMonthDay 1999 6 27) TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q4. Eligible, wishes to take part, signed the form with both agreements: takes part.
#ASSERT `Do I take part in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q4. Did not sign the form: does not take part.
#ASSERT `Do I take part in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q5. A participant who stopped meeting a condition that reduces a week's benefits must tell the Commission as soon as possible.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commission if I stop meeting a condition of entitlement in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q6. A participant is deemed to have claimed the week of Sunday March 9, 1997, inside the period of eligibility.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having claimed benefits for a week in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1997 3 9) TRUE (YearMonthDay 1997 3 2) (YearMonthDay 1997 8 2) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q7. The Commission became aware on May 5, 1997 and decides to end participation: as of that day.
#ASSERT `Can the Commission end my part in Pilot Project No. 1, and from what day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1997 5 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1997 5 5)

-- Q7. Aware, but the Commission does not use its power: no day.
#ASSERT `Can the Commission end my part in Pilot Project No. 1, and from what day` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1997 5 5) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.1 -- Pilot Project No. 5, choosing not to be paid`

-- Q8. The benefit period began March 1, 2000, inside the project (February 9, 2000 to March 14, 2001, invented days), with an indemnity payment: included.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YearMonthDay 2000 3 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 2 9) (YearMonthDay 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q8. The benefit period began and ended before the project: not included.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YearMonthDay 1999 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 1999 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2000 2 9) (YearMonthDay 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q9. The week of Sunday February 6, 2000 is the week in which the section comes into force: the project applies.
#ASSERT `Does Pilot Project No. 5 apply to a week` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 6) (YearMonthDay 2000 2 9) (YearMonthDay 2001 3 14) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q10. A choice made before being paid: deemed to have proved no entitlement for the week.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having proved I am not entitled to benefits for a week I chose not to be paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q10. A choice after payment, the Commission having informed the claimant before: (4)(a), so (3) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having proved I am not entitled to benefits for a week I chose not to be paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q11. A choice after payment, the Commission not having informed the claimant: the benefits paid must be repaid.
#ASSERT `Must I repay benefits I was paid for a week I chose not to be paid for` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q12. Having made a choice and taken it back: paid the benefits to which entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I to be paid my benefits if I take back my choice under Pilot Project No. 5` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Reg 77.2 -- Pilot Project No. 6, increased weeks of benefits (ended in 2006)`

-- Q13. A benefit period established on January 1, 2005 (between June 6, 2004 and June 4, 2006) in a Schedule II.1 region.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q14. Included: the weeks the table gives (45, invented) are the maximum.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) TRUE 45 EQUALS JUST 45

-- Q14. A benefit period established in 2007, after the project: not covered here (the Act's s 12(2) governs).
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2007 1 1) TRUE 45 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regs 77.7 and 77.93 -- Pilot Projects No. 11 and No. 16, a rate based on the 14 highest weeks (ended in 2011 and 2013)`

-- Q15. Established January 1, 2010 in a Schedule II.8 region, not a fisher: included in No. 11.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q15. A claimant to whom the Fishing Regulations apply is excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q16. Established January 1, 2012 in a Schedule II.91 region, not under Part VII.1, not a fisher: included in No. 16.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q17. Included in No. 11 or No. 16: the usual rate rules stop applying.
#ASSERT `Do the usual rate rules stop applying to me under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q18. Included: the qualifying period is read in place of the rate calculation period.
#ASSERT `Which period is used to work out my rate under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2009 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2009 3 29) (YearMonthDay 2008 3 30) (YearMonthDay 2009 3 28) EQUALS (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2008 3 30), (YearMonthDay 2009 3 28))

-- Q19. Ten weeks of 700 and four of 350 are the 14 highest: 8,400 divided by 14.
#ASSERT `What are my weekly insurable earnings under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` (LIST 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 100, 700) 0 EQUALS 600

-- Q20. 1,400 reported for 14 days; one week evidenced at 500; another week takes 900.
#ASSERT `How much of my earnings for a pay period is counted for one week under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` 1400 14 7 TRUE (LIST 500) 7 EQUALS JUST 900

-- Q20. Without evidence a full week of a two-week pay period takes half: 700.
#ASSERT `How much of my earnings for a pay period is counted for one week under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` 1400 14 7 FALSE EMPTY 0 EQUALS JUST 700

§ `Regs 77.8 and 77.94 -- Pilot Projects No. 12 and No. 17, higher allowable earnings (ended in 2011 and 2012)`

-- Q21. Benefit period established June 1, 2009, still running, in a Schedule I region: included in No. 12.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2009 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2009 6 1) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q22. Benefit period established September 1, 2011: included in No. 17.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2011 9 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 9 1) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q23. A rate of 200: 40% is 80, for the week of Sunday July 31, 2011.
#ASSERT `What is the most I may earn in a week under Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 7 31) 200 EQUALS JUST 80

-- Q23. The week of Sunday August 7, 2011 is after the section ceased to have effect: not covered here (the Act's s 19(2) governs).
#ASSERT `What is the most I may earn in a week under Pilot Project No. 12` (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 8 7) 200 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q24. A rate under 188: $75, for the week of Sunday July 29, 2012.
#ASSERT `What is the most I may earn in a week under Pilot Project No. 17` (YearMonthDay 2011 9 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 9 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 7 29) 187 EQUALS JUST 75

§ `Reg 77.91 -- Pilot Project No. 14, extended benefit period and training incentive (ended in 2010)`

-- Q25. Established and begun January 25, 2009; 7 of 10 years; 35 weeks; plan active June 14, 2009; a full-time 20-week course beginning May 31, 2009: included.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q25. 36 weeks of regular benefits is not less than 36.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 36 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q26. 25 weeks of training completed: one week for every five.
#ASSERT `How long is my job-search period under Pilot Project No. 14` 25 EQUALS 5

-- Q27. The last day of attendance was Wednesday September 2, 2009: the job-search period begins on Sunday September 6.
#ASSERT `When does my job-search period under Pilot Project No. 14 begin` (YearMonthDay 2009 9 2) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2009 9 6)

-- Q28. A 30-week course and 25 weeks completed (5 weeks of job-search): extended by 35 weeks.
#ASSERT `By how many weeks is my benefit period extended under Pilot Project No. 14` TRUE 30 25 EQUALS 35

-- Q29. A base of 26 weeks and 10 extra weeks: 36.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 14` TRUE 26 10 FALSE EQUALS 36

-- Q30. A ground to end the referral exists: the extra weeks stop on Sunday September 6, 2009.
#ASSERT `When does the extra-weeks rule of Pilot Project No. 14 stop applying to me` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2009 9 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 9 6)

§ `Reg 77.92 -- Pilot Project No. 15, extended benefits (ended in 2012)`

-- Q31. The rate was under 8.0% for 12 periods; the 12th began on Sunday January 2, 2011: the second Saturday after is January 15, 2011.
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 2) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2011 1 15)

-- Q31. Otherwise the last day is September 15, 2012.
#ASSERT `What is the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 2) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2012 9 15)

-- Q32. Established October 1, 2010 in a Schedule II.6 region; the project ran to September 15, 2012: included.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 2) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q33. The condition of (2)(b)(i) is satisfied: the Commission must publish a notice.
#ASSERT `Will the Commission publish a notice of the day benefit periods stop being established in my region` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q34. Included: the weeks the table gives (52, invented).
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 2) 52 EQUALS JUST 52

§ `Regs 77.95, 77.97 and 77.99 -- Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20, half of your earnings deducted (2012 to 2018)`

-- Q35. The week of Sunday January 6, 2013 is a week of No. 18.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 18` (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q36. The week of Sunday August 2, 2015 is the first week of No. 19.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 19` (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q37. The week of Sunday August 7, 2016 is the first week of No. 20.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q38. Earnings of 600 against 500 weekly insurable earnings: 50% of the first 450 and all of the 150 above it.
#ASSERT `How much of my earnings for a week is deducted under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) TRUE 600 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 375

-- Q38. For the purpose of the waiting period (section 13) the added subsection does not govern.
#ASSERT `How much of my earnings for a week is deducted under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) TRUE 600 500 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q38. A week after all three projects: none governs.
#ASSERT `How much of my earnings for a week is deducted under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` (YearMonthDay 2019 1 6) TRUE 600 500 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q39. A self-employed person: 26,000 divided by 52 is 500; the same deduction.
#ASSERT `How much of my earnings for a week is deducted if I am self-employed under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` (YearMonthDay 2013 1 6) TRUE 600 26000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 375

§ `Regs 77.96, 77.98 and 77.991 -- electing between the two methods of treating your earnings (2012 to 2018)`

-- Q40. Had earnings treated under 77.94(3) in the year to August 4, 2012: may elect.
#ASSERT `May I elect to keep the allowable-earnings method under Pilot Project No. 18` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q41. Last notification October 1, 2012: February 5, 2013 is later than 30 days after.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 18` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 10 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5)

-- Q41. No notification in either period: no deadline is given.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 18` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q42. Told the Commission a day late, with good cause shown: considered made in time.
#ASSERT `Is my election treated as made in time` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 2 6) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Q42. Told the Commission, but no deadline is determined: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is my election treated as made in time` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2013 2 6) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q43. No election for the earlier benefit period, with earnings, and no notification exception: bound for the next.
#ASSERT `Does my failure to elect for an earlier benefit period bind me for the next one under Pilot Project No. 18` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q44. A decision on March 31, 2013: not subject to appeal under section 114.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission's decision on my election closed to appeal under section 114` (YearMonthDay 2013 3 31) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q45. A decision on April 1, 2013: not subject to reconsideration under section 112.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 18 closed to reconsideration under section 112` (YearMonthDay 2013 4 1) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q46. Had the earlier earnings and made every election due: may elect under No. 19.
#ASSERT `May I elect to keep the allowable-earnings method under Pilot Project No. 19` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q47. An election under 77.96 and a last notification on August 2, 2015: it is deemed to apply to the part within No. 19.
#ASSERT `Does my election under section 77.96 also cover my earnings under Pilot Project No. 19` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 8 2) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q48. An election under 77.98(2) for a benefit period that began August 1, 2015: it also covers the part before August 2.
#ASSERT `Does my election under Pilot Project No. 19 also cover my earnings before August 2, 2015` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q49. Last notification May 1, 2016: 30 days later is May 31, 2016, before the closing day of August 6, 2016.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 19` (YearMonthDay 2016 5 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2016 5 31)

-- Q50. No election and earnings: bound for the next benefit period.
#ASSERT `Does my failure to elect for an earlier benefit period bind me for the next one under Pilot Project No. 19` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q51. A decision about an election is not subject to reconsideration under section 112.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 19 closed to reconsideration` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q52. A benefit period from January 1, 2016 to June 30, 2017: the part from August 7, 2016 may carry an election.
#ASSERT `Which part of my benefit period can I apply an election to under Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2016 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2017 6 30) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7), (YearMonthDay 2017 6 30))

-- Q53. An election under 77.98 and a last notification on August 7, 2016: deemed to apply to the part within No. 20.
#ASSERT `Does my election under section 77.98 also cover my earnings under Pilot Project No. 20` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q54. Eligible under 77.98, the benefit period began August 6, 2016 and has not ended, the last notification issued August 7, 2016: may elect.
#ASSERT `May I make an election under Pilot Project No. 20 for a benefit period that began earlier` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2016 8 6) (YearMonthDay 2016 8 7) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q55. Last notification January 1, 2017: 30 days later is January 31, 2017.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 20` (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2017 1 31)

-- Q56. A decision about an election is not subject to reconsideration under section 112.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 20 closed to reconsideration` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q57. May elect, elected, in time, not bound: the allowable-earnings method.
#ASSERT `Which method treats my earnings for the benefit period under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er5 the allowable earnings method of subsection 77.94(3)`

-- Q57. The election was not made in time: the 50% deduction.
#ASSERT `Which method treats my earnings for the benefit period under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er5 the 50 percent deduction method of the pilot project for the period`

§ `Reg 77.992 -- Pilot Project No. 21, increased weeks for seasonal workers (ended in 2021)`

-- Q58. The first week of the present benefit period begins Sunday September 1, 2019; an earlier one began September 2, 2018, 52 weeks before.
#ASSERT `Did an earlier benefit period of mine begin around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 9 2) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q58. An earlier one that began February 4, 2018 is in none of the five periods.
#ASSERT `Did an earlier benefit period of mine begin around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 2 4) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q59. Established September 7, 2014, the first day of the 260 weeks: counts.
#ASSERT `Does an earlier benefit period of mine count as established in the last 260 weeks` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 9 7) FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q59. Established the day before the 260 weeks, with no notification inside them: does not count.
#ASSERT `Does an earlier benefit period of mine count as established in the last 260 weeks` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 9 6) FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q60. Established September 1, 2019 in a Schedule II.92 region, with 3 earlier benefit periods and 2 at the same time of year: included.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) TRUE 3 2 EQUALS TRUE

-- Q60. Only 2 earlier benefit periods: not included.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) TRUE 2 2 EQUALS FALSE

-- Q61. Included: the weeks the table gives (52, invented).
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) TRUE 3 2 52 EQUALS JUST 52

§ `Reg 77.993 -- Pilot Project No. 22, additional weeks for seasonal workers (ended in 2024)`

-- Q62. Established September 10, 2023, meeting the conditions of s 12(2.3): included in No. 22.
#ASSERT `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 22` (YearMonthDay 2023 9 10) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q63. Schedule II.94 is read in place of Schedule V.
#ASSERT `Which schedule is read in place of Schedule V for Pilot Project No. 22` EQUALS "Schedule II.94 of the Employment Insurance Regulations"

§ `Reg 77.994 -- Pilot Project No. 23, additional hours after natural disasters (ended in 2025)`

-- Q64. An initial claim in T0E 1E0; a benefit period begun August 4, 2024 and still running when the section came into force (October 1, 2024, invented): 300 additional hours.
#ASSERT `How many additional hours of insurable employment am I deemed to have under Pilot Project No. 23` TRUE "T0E 1E0" TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 8 4) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 8 4) (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 10 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 300

-- Q64. A postal code that is not one of the three: no additional hours.
#ASSERT `How many additional hours of insurable employment am I deemed to have under Pilot Project No. 23` TRUE "T0E 1E1" TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 8 4) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 8 4) (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 10 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0

-- Q65. The additional hours count for subsection 28(4) of the Act.
#ASSERT `Do my additional hours count as hours of insurable employment for a given provision` TRUE "subsection 28(4) of the Act" EQUALS TRUE

-- Q65. Section 7 of the Act is not on the list.
