-- Q75. Extended; ceasing to be a long-tenured worker alone does not end the extra weeks.
#ASSERT `Do my additional weeks stay payable if I stop being a long-tenured worker` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Regs 78 and 79 -- asking the Commission to reconsider a decision`

-- Q76. A written request with name, number, address and phone, the decision date and reasons; no fax, no email, nothing new to add: complete.
#ASSERT `Does my request for reconsideration contain what regulation 78 requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q76. The claimant has an email address and the request leaves it out.
#ASSERT `Does my request for reconsideration contain what regulation 78 requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q77. Filed at the email address the website provides.
#ASSERT `Did I file my request for reconsideration the way the Commission's website provides` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q78. A request has been made: the Commission must decide it without delay.
#ASSERT `Must the Commission decide my request for reconsideration without delay` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q79. The regulation gives no number of days: whether 90 days is too long is not covered.
#ASSERT `Has the Commission taken too long to decide my request for reconsideration` 90 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regs 80 to 82 -- benefits held back while the Commission appeals`

-- Q80. The decision was given March 1, 2020 and the Commission appealed on March 22, 2020, the 21st day, on a ground of error in law.
#ASSERT `Are my benefits held back because the Commission appealed the tribunal's decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 22) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q80. Appealed on March 23, 2020, a day too late.
#ASSERT `Are my benefits held back because the Commission appealed the tribunal's decision` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 23) TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q81. The Commission applied for judicial review and it is not yet determined: held back.
#ASSERT `Are my benefits held back because the Commission applied for judicial review` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q82. The claim that is the object of the decision is caught.
#ASSERT `Is my claim caught by a decision that a provision is ultra vires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q83. A General Division decision under appeal, the appeal not yet determined: held back.
#ASSERT `Are my benefits held back because the Commission appealed a decision that a provision is ultra vires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q83. The Appeal Division decided and declared it ultra vires, but the Commission has not applied for judicial review: the stoppage ended (the reading taken).
#ASSERT `Are my benefits held back because the Commission appealed a decision that a provision is ultra vires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q84. The Commission applied for judicial review of a decision declaring a provision ultra vires; not yet determined: held back.
#ASSERT `Are my benefits held back because the Commission applied for judicial review of a decision that a provision is ultra vires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Reg 88 -- benefits held back while a ruling on my insurable hours is pending`

-- Q85. The officer's ruling final January 10, 2020; the Minister's decision March 5; the Tax Court's June 20: the later day is June 20, 2020.
#ASSERT `On what day do the rulings on my insurable hours become final` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 5) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 6 20) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 6 20)

-- Q85. The officer's ruling is not yet final: no day.
#ASSERT `On what day do the rulings on my insurable hours become final` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q86. The rulings became final on March 5, 2020: on March 4 no benefits are payable for the hour.
#ASSERT `Are benefits not payable for the hours under ruling on a given day` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 4) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q86. The claimant qualifies on other hours: (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Are benefits not payable for the hours under ruling on a given day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 4) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Reg 89 -- my Social Insurance Number`

-- Q87. In insurable employment, required to have a number, not yet applied: must apply.
#ASSERT `Must I apply to the Commission to be registered for a Social Insurance Number` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q88. Employment begins March 2, 2020: apply by March 5.
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply to be registered for a Social Insurance Number` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2020 3 5)

-- Q89. Applied on March 5, the last day.
#ASSERT `Did I apply to be registered in time` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 5) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q90. The employer must ask by March 5.
#ASSERT `By what day must my employer ask me for my Social Insurance Number` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 5)

-- Q91. Employed before being registered, number received March 20: tell the employer by March 23.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 23)

-- Q92. Registered at the start; told the employer on March 5, the last day.
#ASSERT `Did I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number in time` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 5) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q93. The employer cannot ascertain the number: it must report by March 8, six days after.
#ASSERT `By what day must my employer report to the Commission if it cannot ascertain my Social Insurance Number` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 8)

-- Q94. The validity of the number was extended: must tell the employer.
#ASSERT `Must I tell my employer that my Social Insurance Number or its validity has changed` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q95. Informed of the change on March 10: tell the employer by March 13.
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell my employer of the change in my Social Insurance Number` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2020 3 13)

-- Q96. Told the employer on March 13, the last day.
#ASSERT `Did I tell my employer of the change in time` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 13) EQUALS TRUE

§ `Regs 90 and 91 -- giving the Commission information and claiming by telephone or online`

-- Q97. Information given to the Commission for the purposes of the Act must be in a form and manner it approves.
#ASSERT `Must information I give the Commission be in a form and manner it approves` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q98. The form and manner used is not one the Commission approved.
#ASSERT `Is the information I gave provided as the Commission requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q99. A claim by telephone with the information section 50 requires: deemed made.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having made my claim when I claimed by telephone or online` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q100. The same claim: deemed to have supplied the printout's answers.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having answered the questions when I claimed by telephone or online` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q101. An initial claim by telephone: Social Insurance Number and date of birth.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having signed my claim when I claimed by telephone or online` `er5 an initial claim for benefits` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q101. A claim for a week: Social Insurance Number and personal identification number.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having signed my claim when I claimed by telephone or online` `er5 a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q102. Received and recorded on March 9, 2020: deemed made that day.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim by telephone or online treated as made` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 9) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 9)

-- Q103. Sections 38 and 135 apply to a declaration made electronically.
#ASSERT `Do the false-statement provisions apply to a declaration I make electronically` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q104. A person who knowingly tries to interfere with the systems can be refused access.
#ASSERT `Can I be refused access to the Commission's electronic systems if I try to interfere with them` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q105. The attempt counts as an act or omission of sections 38(1) and 135(1).
#ASSERT `Does my attempt to interfere with the electronic systems count as an offence of section 38 or 135` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Reg 92 -- direct deposit of my benefits`

-- Q106. Sections 2 and 4 to 8 of the Direct Deposit Regulations apply.
#ASSERT `Which sections of the Direct Deposit Regulations apply to me` EQUALS LIST 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8

-- Q107. An active account in the claimant's name in a Canadian institution: deposited directly.
#ASSERT `Will my benefits be deposited directly to my bank account` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q107. Refused access to the direct deposit systems under (7): no direct deposit.
#ASSERT `Will my benefits be deposited directly to my bank account` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q108. The claimant is responsible for the accuracy of the data they supplied.
#ASSERT `Am I responsible for the accuracy of the bank details I gave` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q109. Both certified extracts and no evidence to the contrary: evidence of the transfer and payment.
#ASSERT `Do the Commission's documents prove my benefits were deposited` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Q109. With evidence to the contrary the regulation does not say what they are worth.
#ASSERT `Do the Commission's documents prove my benefits were deposited` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q110. To end the direct deposit the claimant must notify the Commission.
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Commission to stop my direct deposit` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q111. Wishing to end it is not enough: not ended until notified.
#ASSERT `Has my direct deposit ended` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q112. Sections 38 and 135 apply to a declaration made about payment.
#ASSERT `Do the false-statement provisions apply to a declaration I make about my payment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q113. A person who knowingly tries to interfere with the direct deposit systems can be refused access.
#ASSERT `Can I be refused access to the direct deposit systems if I try to interfere with them` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q114. The attempt counts as an act or omission of sections 38(1) and 135(1).
#ASSERT `Does my attempt to interfere with the direct deposit systems count as an offence of section 38 or 135` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q115. Not advised otherwise, an active account whose number was given, the institution notified a change: the Commission may redirect.
#ASSERT `May the Commission redirect my direct deposit to another account` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
